  "policy": "NPU prefill retains calibrated Q8 KV; only decode rows become TurboQuant4. No prefix recompression. Q8 segments after TQ decode are supported.",
  "default_enabled": false,
  "acceptance": {
    "requires_speed_and_memory_net_gain": true,
    "met": false,
    "reason": "Memory reduction and removal of prefill overhead confirmed. Whole-model decode remains slower (latest paired hybrid 52.0294 versus Q8 50.6127 ms/token in sequential natural-generation runs). D256 attention-only long-context wins vary with run; actual model global D512 remains slower than Q8. Speed+memory criterion is not met."
  },
  "root_causes": [
    "The first hybrid reader processed Q8 prefix tiles using a new per-tile FP32 online softmax rather than the tuned existing native Q8 head pipeline: measured total attention 25.365 ms/token versus 5.597 ms/token for Q8 at 961 prompt tokens.",
    "Initial hybrid prefill scanned/converted all FP32 QKV before Q8 calibration/packing: 105.700 ms summed conversion/check time in the 961-token trace.",
    "Q8 working tiles and masters were allocated each layer; initial full payload initialization and allocation were exposed in prefill. Existing Q8 registered its caches at model load.",
    "Q8 and TQ initially dispatched separately and merged normalized contexts through log2-sum-exp. Query quantization used scalar double arithmetic and per-probability division.",
    "Natural output differences change MoE expert access. Fixed-token replay is necessary to reduce that comparison confound; thermal/I/O still vary.",
    "Packed 4-bit storage reduces bytes but requires Hadamard query rotation, codebook lookup, integer score reconstruction, value unpacking and inverse rotation. At short history these costs dominate the saved traffic.",
    "MoE uses a fixed target of 34 cached experts per layer. Released KV memory is not automatically reused for experts. Testing target 38 reduced expert misses but did not improve measured end-to-end speed.",
    "For D512/GQA8 global layers the original scheduler used one query per KV scan, decoding the same packed KV eight times per head. Byte scores alone did not fix this: standalone 32K D512 hybrid was 14.64 ms versus Q8 5.44 ms."
  ],
  "changes": [
    "Transfer Q8 masters/scales directly into persistent prefix ownership; remove FP32 KV retention and prefill TQ encoding.",
    "Consume Q8 prefixes with the existing native Q8 kernel; preserve quantized values while changing only byte layout on first read. Vectorize the full-tile layout transform.",
    "Reuse one immutable exp table per cache shape instead of initializing it for every layer/chunk.",
    "Run the TQ suffix consumer inside the Q8 head worker for supported v81 D256/GQA2/eight-KV-head shapes; preserve a generic path for other shapes.",
    "Merge unnormalized contexts with maximum and exponent sums; no logarithm is needed. Vectorize query scaling/packing and reuse probability reciprocals.",
    "Calibrate/pack Q8 directly from resident FP32 QKV with row-local FP16 rounding, preserving baseline Q8 prefill outputs without full FP16 KV intermediates.",
    "Initialize only padding/tails that a fresh append does not overwrite; reuse Q8 WH computation tiles between layers. Free them at decode/reset/close.",
    "Prepare the TQ-dependent resident graph in the model preparation lifecycle; this moves one-time setup, and is not claimed as a compute speedup.",
    "Initialize inactive calibration worker lanes to neutral values: short prefill chunks previously merged uninitialized maxima/ranges.",
    "Report Q8 plus TQ payload and actual prefill workspace ownership; reject writes into immutable Q8 regions and invalid/released cache ranges.",
    "On prefix-backed single-token decode, consume the original current K/V and pack an owned copy asynchronously after attention, overlapping later projection/MoE work. Join before subsequent cache access/reset/free.",
    "Vectorize P15 probability packing and reconstruct Q12 centroid byte planes in groups of four dimension pairs.",
    "For supported long global D256/KV8/GQA2 and D512/KV2/GQA8 shapes with at least 4096 packed history rows, use byte query/centroid score computation; persistent 4-bit codebook/storage are unchanged. Other shapes, short/sliding and packed-only paths retain Q12 score computation.",
    "Pair two GQA queries for D512 as well as D256 so packed K/V interpretation is shared. Standalone D512 32K hybrid improved from 14.64 to 9.36 ms, but remains slower than Q8; no full-model speed claim."
  ],
